
-- time-scheduling.pgm - Time & Scheduling Management Component
-- Essential component for handling time queries, scheduling, and temporal conversations
-- Covers time awareness, appointments, deadlines, and calendar operations

-- Time Queries
Recognizer "what time is it"
	Remember "User asked for current time"
	Option Say "I don't have access to real-time data, but you can check your device's clock!"
	Option Say "You can check the time on your phone or computer - I don't have clock access."

Recognizer "what's the time"
	Remember "User asked for time"
	Option Say "I can't see the current time, but your device should show it!"

Recognizer "current time"
	Remember "User wants current time"
	Option Say "Check your system clock - I don't have real-time access."

-- Scheduling Requests
Recognizer "schedule a meeting"
	Remember "User wants to schedule meeting"
	Option Say "I'd love to help with scheduling! What meeting details do you have in mind?"
	Option Say "Great idea! What time works best for your meeting?"

Recognizer "book an appointment"
	Remember "User wants appointment"
	Option Say "I can help you think through appointment scheduling. What type of appointment?"

Recognizer "set a reminder"
	Remember "User wants reminder"
	Option Say "Good thinking! What would you like to be reminded about?"
	Option Say "Reminders are so helpful! What should I help you remember?"

-- Time Periods - Today/Tomorrow
Recognizer "today"
	Remember "User mentioned today"
	Option Say "Today's a great day to get things done! What are you planning?"
	Option Say "What's on your agenda for today?"

Recognizer "tomorrow"
	Remember "User mentioned tomorrow"
	Option Say "Tomorrow's coming up fast! Are you planning ahead?"
	Option Say "Planning for tomorrow is always smart. What's coming up?"

Recognizer "yesterday"
	Remember "User mentioned yesterday"
	Option Say "Yesterday's experiences often inform today's decisions. What happened?"

